        <summary>Read the story as text</summary>
        <div class="stack"><h3>Chapter 1: The Maverick</h3><ol class="gn-text"><li><b>1. 13 years of saying yes</b> Thirteen years in corporate life. I said yes to every opportunity. Every project. Every challenge. Solving problems, learning fast, taking on more.</li><li><b>2. The restructure</b> Then came the restructure. The landscape changed. Uncertainty grew. And my autonomy, the thing I valued most, started to disappear.</li><li><b>3. The leaving drinks question</b> At the leaving drinks, a colleague asked: &quot;So, what&#x27;s your exit plan?&quot; The honest answer? I didn&#x27;t really have one. But I knew I wanted the community to own their future, not some investor looking to extract value.</li></ol><h3>Chapter 2: The First Hive</h3><ol class="gn-text"><li><b>4. The 2010 platform</b> In 2010, I built a platform to bring skilled people together. A place to connect talent, ideas and opportunities.</li><li><b>5. A £20–30k investment</b> I invested £20–30k to get it off the ground. But it didn&#x27;t gain the traction I&#x27;d hoped for. It was a setback. Not a defeat.</li><li><b>6. Rethink and keep going</b> So I stepped back, rethought the approach and kept going. The model was still strong; it just didn&#x27;t need a complex platform. I could deliver it using everyday tools, focusing on people, partnerships and real-world collaboration.</li></ol><h3>Chapter 3: Assembling the Team</h3><ol class="gn-text"><li><b>7. University of Greenwich</b> We put the model into practice at UoG, creating pop-up teams to solve real challenges for businesses in the South East. It showed what was possible when the right people come together.</li><li><b>8. Alan joins</b> Alan joined while completing his MBA, bringing experience, structure and a calm, steady perspective. A hugely important ally in the journey.</li><li><b>9. The Swarm</b> Together we launched The Swarm, bringing students and diverse talent together to work on real projects. Fresh thinking. New perspectives. A true collaboration.</li><li><b>10. Take Your Shot (with Slinky and Sony)</b> We created Take Your Shot with Slinky and Sony, giving emerging talent a platform to develop their skills and showcase their creativity.</li><li><b>11. A BAFTA nominee</b> That journey led to an incredible moment: one of the talented individuals we supported went on to win awards and a BAFTA nomination.</li></ol><h3>Chapter 4: SkillsHiveX</h3><ol class="gn-text"><li><b>12. 15 years of building</b> Fifteen years of building, learning and adapting. Creating pop-up teams, connecting skills and helping great people do meaningful work together.</li><li><b>13. A community that stewards itself</b> Today, SkillsHiveX is a community of people and teams who create value together. It&#x27;s bigger than any one of us: a self-stewarding ecosystem that opens up opportunities and helps more people thrive.</li><li><b>14. Come and be part of it</b> This is just the beginning. Come and be part of a growing community, where different skills, experiences and perspectives create real opportunities. A brighter together.</li></ol></div>
